Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns for the task  
(event level unless otherwise noted)

• event_date : date partition – filter rows that happened between 2018‑07‑02 and 2018‑07‑30 (we need 14 follow‑up days).  
• event_name : find the “quickplay …” events and “session_start”.  
• event_timestamp : (µs since epoch) – can be used to calculate exact day differences if needed.  
• user_pseudo_id : stable anonymous GA4 user id – cohort & retention key.  
• event_params : ARRAY<STRUCT> – contains extra dimensions; for quick‑play the sub key that tells the exact quick‑play type is stored here (we will look for it).  
    • key = 'quickplay_event_type'  (or similar) → value.string_value holds the readable quick‑play type.  
• _TABLE_SUFFIX (pseudo‑column when using the wildcard table name events_*) : lets us pick only the daily tables we need.

Typical conditions that will be used  

1. _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180702' AND '20180716'        -- build the initial cohort  
2. _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180716' AND '20180730'        -- look 14 days later  
3. event_name = 'session_start'                           -- users who opened a session  
4. event_name LIKE 'quickplay%'                           -- rows that are quick‑play events  
5. quickplay_type IS NOT NULL                             -- make sure we really found the type  

